<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Invasion of the Waikato</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1863">1863</a>–<a href="/years/1864">1864</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Invasion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waikato">Waikato</a> was the largest campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> Wars, fought in 1863–1864 by British and colonial forces against the Māori King Movement in the Waikato region of the North Island. After battles at Rangiriri and Ōrākau the King Movement withdrew south, and the government confiscated large areas of Māori land.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/invasion-of-the-waikato.jpg" alt="Invasion of the Waikato" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Cowan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ngati_maniapoto_survivors_of_the_war.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
